codex
`answers.csv` contains only a header, so it provides no new labels. I will use the selected rule in `CANDIDATES.md`: when confidence is below 0.4, add urgency to impact and cap impact at 1. I will preserve the existing model and add ReLU layers before it. A ReLU network needs a narrow transition at the confidence threshold; I will document that limit.
hook: PreToolUse
hook: PreToolUse Completed
apply patch
patch: completed
$WSROOT/large/s1/sol-query0w-r2/step4/edit_model.py
diff --git a/edit_model.py b/edit_model.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7ef591157acc3d9fcd53b6c378cf6795aac1f4df
--- /dev/null
+++ b/edit_model.py
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+"""Build a manually specified ReLU input correction. No training or fitting."""
+import numpy as np
+from model import load, save
+
+
+original = load("model_in.json")
+# Powers of two make scaling of the confidence threshold exact in binary64.
+# The gate reaches one within 2**-40 below the threshold.
+scale = float(2**40)
+
+# Layer A: copy the nonnegative inputs, r = ReLU(i+u-1),
+# and g = ReLU(scale*(0.4-c)).
+wa = np.zeros((20, 22))
+wa[:, :20] = np.eye(20)
+wa[0, 20] = wa[1, 20] = 1
+wa[4, 21] = -scale
+ba = np.zeros(22)
+ba[20] = -1
+ba[21] = 0.4 * scale
+
+# Layer B: t = ReLU(u-r) = min(u, 1-i), q = ReLU(t-g).
+wb = np.zeros((22, 22))
+wb[:20, :20] = np.eye(20)
+wb[1, 20:22] = 1
+wb[20, 20:22] = -1
+wb[21, 21] = -1
+bb = np.zeros(22)
+
+# Layer C: compute the added impact separately to preserve the original
+# inputs exactly when the gate is zero: a = ReLU(t-q) = min(t,g).
+wc = np.zeros((22, 21))
+wc[:20, :20] = np.eye(20)
+wc[20, 20] = 1
+wc[21, 20] = -1
+bc = np.zeros(21)
+
+# Layer D: replace impact by i+a. All other inputs pass through unchanged.
+wd = np.zeros((21, 20))
+wd[:20, :] = np.eye(20)
+wd[20, 0] = 1
+bd = np.zeros(20)
+
+save([(wa, ba), (wb, bb), (wc, bc), (wd, bd)] + original,
+     "model_out.json")

